Hivra
=====
Hivra (https://github.com/ashneil12/hivra-hub) is a fork of MonoCode
(https://github.com/hardbeat920/monocode), MIT. The projects it learns from are listed in
docs/hivra/SOURCES.md and in the app (Settings, About, Credits).

Third-party components Hivra adds:

- UniiChat's summary tree (Memory.ts, prompt.txt)
  Source: https://github.com/VictorTaelin/UniiChat
  License: Apache-2.0
  Copyright 2026 Higher Order Company
  Used in: src/features/monos/model/monoTree.ts, monoTreePrompt.txt
  Ported and changed; see src/features/monos/model/monoTree.NOTICE.md.

- react-day-picker
  Source: https://github.com/gpbl/react-day-picker
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) 2014-2026 Giampaolo Bellavite and contributors
  Used in: src/features/pages/ui/CalendarBlock.tsx
  npm package, restyled with the app's theme tokens.

- Tremor BarList
  Source: https://github.com/tremorlabs/tremor
  License: Apache-2.0
  Copyright Tremor Labs and the Tremor contributors
  Used in: src/features/pages/ui/PagesView.tsx
  Restyled copy of the component, no package.

- firstmate's contract text
  Source: https://github.com/kunchenguid/firstmate
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) 2026 Kun Chen
  Used in: src/features/firstmate/vendor/firstmate-contract.md, src/features/firstmate/contract.md, src/features/firstmate/model/brief.ts, src-tauri/src/firstmate/
  Hard rules, delivery path, brief fill, isolation check, status lines, steering inbox and project-memory rule, vendored verbatim (WP-10), with the MIT licence in src/features/firstmate/vendor/LICENSE. A one-line binding follows each block where Hivra has no status file, inbox directory or captain address.

- Puppetmaster's failure classification and retry budget
  Source: https://github.com/professorpalmer/Puppetmaster
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) 2026 Cary
  Used in: src/features/crew/model/failure.ts, src/features/crew/model/budget.ts, src-tauri/src/crew/failure.rs, src-tauri/src/crew/budget.rs
  failure.py and failure_policy.py translated to TypeScript and Rust (WP-13). The checks and their order are the original's. A boolean is not a retry count.

- Puppetmaster's session lease and idempotent launch key
  Source: https://github.com/professorpalmer/Puppetmaster
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) 2026 Cary
  Used in: host/firstmate/lease.ts, host/firstmate/records.ts
  session_lease.py and create_or_get_job translated to TypeScript (WP-60). The same launch key returns the same worker; the same key with a different request is a conflict. A live holder is not replaced, and a dead one counts as released. Node's flock is per-process, so the lease is held in the host process as well as a pid file.

- pstack (default plugin)
  Source: https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) 2026 Lauren Tan
  Used in: src-tauri/plugins/pstack
  pstack 0.15.36 copied unchanged from cursor/plugins at commit 6ea74587, less its Cursor-only parts (agents, automations, .cursor-plugin), images and a test corpus; embedded in the app and installed once per data folder as Hivra's default plugin, with its LICENSE (WP-41).

- pstack (test fixture)
  Source: https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) 2026 Lauren Tan
  Used in: src-tauri/src/plugins/fixtures/pstack
  Copied unchanged from cursor/plugins at commit 6ea74587 as a test fixture, with its LICENSE (WP-30).

- council-of-high-intelligence personas and protocol
  Source: https://github.com/0xnyk/council-of-high-intelligence
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) 2026 nyk
  Used in: src/features/council/personas, src/features/council/model/prompts.ts
  The 18 council personas and the blind, cross-exam, stance and chairman prompts, copied with the MIT notice (WP-23).

- Mercury's soul migration check
  Source: https://github.com/cosmicstack-labs/mercury-agent
  License: MIT
  Copyright © 2026 Cosmic Stack
  Used in: src/features/monos/model/vendor/mercurySoul.ts
  needsMigration and normalizeSoulText copied from src/soul/identity.ts (WP-21). The legacy template list is passed in, because Mercury's stored souls are Cosmic Stack text and are not included.

- agent-desktop skill
  Source: https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-desktop
  License: Apache-2.0
  The upstream files do not carry a separate copyright line (Apache-2.0)
  Used in: plugins/desktop-control/skills/agent-desktop/SKILL.md
  Vendored from skills/agent-desktop/SKILL.md at agent-desktop 1.1.0, with Hivra's gate and consent rules added (WP-44)

- Orbit trash
  Source: https://github.com/coollabsio/orbit
  License: Apache-2.0
  The upstream files do not carry a separate copyright line (Apache-2.0)
  Used in: src-tauri/src/trash.rs, src/features/trash
  Page and task trash rules from apps/server/src/repositories/pages.rs, tasks.rs, sub_issues.rs and workspaces.rs (a batch shares one deleted_at and one trashed_with, a 30-day purge, a restored child of a still-trashed parent comes back at the top level), translated onto one trash_items ledger because Orbit's SQL is sqlx against tasks and pages tables Hivra does not have (WP-76).

- Raven's chat importer
  Source: https://github.com/EverMind-AI/Raven
  License: Apache-2.0
  The upstream files do not carry a separate copyright line (Apache-2.0)
  Used in: src/features/historyImport, src-tauri/src/history_import.rs
  Translated line by line from the importer. Tool noise is dropped, provenance is stricter, and a preview reads only the header (WP-50).

- Agent Zero's migrate-agents preview
  Source: https://github.com/agent0ai/agent-zero
  License: MIT
  Copyright (c) 2025 Agent Zero, s.r.o.
  Used in: src/features/historyImport
  The chat preview and the Claude, Codex and Hermes readers, translated line by line. A preview counts from the header only (WP-50).

