The native UI uses Zed Industries' GPUI framework through gpui-pre and
gpui-pre-platform 0.3.9 (Zed snapshot
93d745668805029476e6d7fbb19652116fed51de), licensed under Apache-2.0.
Copyright 2022 - 2025 Zed Industries, Inc.
The native composer in crates/monocode-gpui/src/input.rs adapts text input
plumbing from that snapshot's GPUI examples/input.rs.
Source: https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/blob/93d745668805029476e6d7fbb19652116fed51de/crates/gpui/examples/input.rs
License: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0
License text: docs/native/LICENSE-GPUI-APACHE

Native Mermaid previews use mermaid-rs-renderer 0.3.1, licensed under MIT.
Copyright (c) 2026 mermaid-rs-renderer contributors.
Source: https://github.com/1jehuang/mermaid-rs-renderer
License text: docs/native/LICENSE-MERMAID-MIT

Native window and sidebar glyphs reuse Monocode's Hugeicons Stroke Rounded set
from @hugeicons/core-free-icons 4.3.0, copyright Hugeicons, licensed under MIT.
Source: https://github.com/hugeicons/hugeicons

vendor/gpui-pre-apple contains gpui-pre-apple 0.3.9 (Zed snapshot
93d745668805029476e6d7fbb19652116fed51de), copyright Zed Industries,
licensed under Apache-2.0 (license included). Monocode modifications include
source-over alpha blending, backdrop blur, edge fades, text reveal, rounded
clipping, project-background compositing, shadow clipping, and font-weight
matching in the text system.
Source: https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/tree/93d745668805029476e6d7fbb19652116fed51de/crates/gpui_apple
License text: vendor/gpui-pre-apple/LICENSE-APACHE

vendor/gpui-pre, vendor/gpui-pre-linux and vendor/gpui-pre-windows contain
gpui-pre 0.3.9 components from the same Zed snapshot, copyright Zed Industries,
licensed under Apache-2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE included in each directory).
The GPUI SVG renderer also exposes an image-free parsing mode for untrusted
generated Mermaid diagrams, preserving normal image resolution for other SVGs.
Monocode removes the unused zed-scap dependency and its feature links from their
manifests, and rejects screen-capture builds in gpui-pre/build.rs pending license
review. The retained framework code remains Apache-2.0.
Unused upstream examples and their demo assets are omitted, together with four
upstream SVG tests requiring font fixtures absent from the published crate.
The small EXIF image regression fixture is retained under tests/assets.

Native chat file icons and the Dark+ token palette reuse the React UI's
react-material-icon-theme 1.2.0 and @shikijs/themes assets. Their MIT license
notices are included alongside the assets in crates/monocode-gpui/assets.

The native editor's analysis and formatting bundles reuse CodeMirror, Lezer,
the Replit Svelte grammar and Prettier under their MIT licenses. Package versions and complete license notices are included in
crates/monocode-gpui/assets/native-editor.LICENSE.txt. The bundle is generated
from scripts/native-editor and the retained React editor language, syntax,
lint, typing and Git hunk implementations. Prettier dependency notices are
included alongside the package licenses.

